# `reporting/presentations/` — Slide decks

One folder per talk, named by **date + venue**: `YYYY-MM-venue/`
(e.g. `2026-07-lab-meeting/`). The date is not decoration — a talk you gave is a
historical record, so decks are dated and **not edited in place** afterward. Give
a new talk → new folder.

## Format
**Beamer** (LaTeX). Beamer brings its own document class, so — unlike the paper
and poster — the deck does **not** load `_assets/lab.cls`. What it *does* share with
them is the **font policy** (`_assets/fonts.tex`, `\input` for the sans family) and
the **generated theme colours** (`_assets/theme-colors-dark.tex`). See
`example/slides.tex` and build with `make -C .. slides`. Whatever the format:

- **Figures come from `../../results/figures/dark/`** (transparent background, sits
  on any slide color). Reference them; don't paste-and-forget.
- Record the results git SHA / {{ data_versioning }} rev the deck was built from,
  so you can trace which figure version you presented.

Keep old decks. They are cheap to store and priceless when someone asks "what did
you show at that meeting?"
